Package: hermiteStats
Type: Package
Title: Distribution-Robust Statistics via Hermite Polynomial Quantile Modeling
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Wolfgang", "Lenhard", 
           email = "wolfgang.lenhard@uni-wuerzburg.de", 
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8184-6889")),
    person("Alexandra", "Lenhard", 
           email = "lenhard@psychometrica.de",
           role = c("aut"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8680-4381"))
  )
Description: Provides distribution-robust estimation and statistical inference
    for distributional moments, bivariate correlations and standardized mean
    differences (effect sizes) without requiring distributional assumptions.
    Traditional robust methods often achieve stability by trimming,
    Winsorizing, or rank conversion, thereby changing the target estimand and
    discarding authentic tail variance. The methods in this package map
    empirical data to standard normal scores via rank-based inverse-normal
    transformation (Normal Quantile Transformation), model the empirical
    quantile functions using regularized monotone polynomials, and extract
    distributional moments in exact closed algebraic form using monic
    Probabilists' Hermite polynomials and Isserlis' (1918)
    <doi:10.1093/biomet/12.1-2.134> theorem. For bivariate data, the joint
    covariance is computed analytically either completely without prior
    assumptions or under a latent Gaussian copula via Mehler's (1866)
    <doi:10.1515/crll.1866.66.161> identity. Building on this engine, the
    package further provides a suite of distribution-robust two-sample and
    paired hypothesis tests: permutation tests (with approximate analytical
    alternatives) for regularized mean and median differences, permutation
    tests for differences in scale, asymmetry, and tail weight based on
    Parseval-standardized Hermite shape indices, and a unified distributional
    profile test that evaluates all five aspects jointly with
    Westfall and Young (1993, ISBN:9780471557616) step-down multiplicity
    control and omnibus testing.
